LESSON 14: LIFTING STATE UP - HANDS-ON - RANDOM QUOTE APP
================================================================================
PART 1: OVERVIEW OF THE LESSON
================================================================================

WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS LESSON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This lesson applies the shared-state / "Lifting State Up" pattern to the
Random Quote App.

You will understand:

• Refactoring the Quote App around a shared state owner

• Keeping shared quote state in the App component

• Extracting presentation and action components

• Passing state and handlers through props

• Coordinating multiple state variables

• Enabling communication between components

• Restructuring the component hierarchy

• Applying the lifting-state pattern in practice

• Testing the refactored application

• Comparing before and after implementations

• Building a more scalable Quote App architecture


WHY THIS HANDS-ON LESSON IS IMPORTANT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hands-on refactoring is useful because:

• Reinforces Theory
  - Applies shared-state concepts to an existing application

• Builds Practical Experience
  - Demonstrates how component responsibilities can be separated

• Shows Real Refactoring
  - Starts with working code and restructures it

• Improves Problem-Solving
  - Helps identify state owners and component responsibilities

• Improves Code Organization
  - Separates state, presentation, actions, and layout

• Improves Maintainability
  - Changes become easier to locate

• Supports Scalability
  - New components/features can be added more cleanly

• Improves Testing
  - Smaller components can be tested independently

• Prepares for Advanced Patterns
  - Provides a foundation for Context and useReducer


