IMPORTANT CONCEPTUAL NOTE
================================================================================

The starting Random Quote App ALREADY stores:

• quote
• loading
• error
• color

inside App.

QuoteCard receives those values through props.

Therefore, state is already located at the common parent level.

So this lesson is not literally:

"Move state from QuoteCard to App."

Instead, the practical refactoring is:

BEFORE:

App
 ├── Shared State
 ├── Business Logic
 ├── Effects
 ├── Layout
 ├── Buttons
 └── QuoteCard


AFTER:

App
 ├── Shared State
 ├── Business Logic
 ├── Effects
 │
 └── Child Components
      ├── QuoteContainer
      ├── QuoteDisplay
      └── QuoteActions


The architectural principle remains the same:

SHARED STATE STAYS IN THE COMMON OWNER,
WHILE SPECIALIZED UI RESPONSIBILITIES MOVE INTO CHILD COMPONENTS.


